<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<!--
    ONE radio clock, ONE look (UI-tweaks round 4, AD / Contract K2).

    The radio clock is DEVICE-WIDE state: `TI` is answered in every mode and
    `TIME`+`DAT`+`DAY` set the same value from anywhere. Round 3 shipped it
    twice — a "Time" card on the HOP Operate pane and a "Radio clock" row on
    Radio settings — with two different looks over two different VMs. This
    ContentView is the single component both placements now use:

      Radio settings -> Settings tab, and Mode settings -> HOP tab.

    Same headings, same Option-B confirmed display, same button text, and the
    SAME state underneath (DeviceSettingsViewModel, a DI singleton bound in
    code-behind — the ConsoleSection house pattern), so the two placements can
    never disagree.

    Constitution: the TOD display is ONE-WAY from the confirmed mirror and
    reads "—" until the radio reports a TIME line; pressing Set moves NOTHING
    on screen — only the radio's own answer does.

    Gating: Ready ALONE. The clock is not mode state, so in the HOP settings
    pane this card sits OUTSIDE the pane's confirmed-HOP grey gate (K2), and
    the button's own CanExecute (session Ready) is the only gate either
    placement applies.
-->
<ContentView xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/dotnet/2021/maui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2009/xaml"
             xmlns:vm="clr-namespace:Falcon.App.Core.ViewModels;assembly=Falcon.App.Core"
             x:Class="Falcon.App.Views.SettingsParts.DeviceClockView"
             x:DataType="vm:DeviceSettingsViewModel">
    <Border Style="{StaticResource Card}">
        <VerticalStackLayout Spacing="10">
            <Label Text="Radio clock" Style="{StaticResource CardHeading}" />
            <Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto,Auto" ColumnSpacing="6">
                <Label Grid.Column="0" VerticalOptions="Center" Style="{StaticResource Caption}"
                       Text="Radio TOD" />
                <Border Grid.Column="1" Style="{StaticResource ValueDisplay}"
                        WidthRequest="{StaticResource ValueWidthWide}"
                        SemanticProperties.Description="Radio time of day reported by the radio">
                    <Label Style="{StaticResource ValueDisplayText}"
                           Text="{Binding RadioTodText}" />
                </Border>
                <Button Grid.Column="2" Text="Set from device clock" Style="{StaticResource Segment}"
                        Command="{Binding SetTimeFromDeviceCommand}"
                        SemanticProperties.Description="Set the radio clock from this device (sends TIME, DAT and DAY)" />
            </Grid>
        </VerticalStackLayout>
    </Border>
</ContentView>
